<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gongmin of Goryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1330–1374</span> · Also known as King Gongmin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gongmin was king of Goryeo from 1351 to 1374. Raised at the Yuan court and married to the Mongol princess Noguk, he turned against Yuan control as the dynasty weakened, purging the pro-Mongol Gi family in 1356 and recovering northern lands. His later reforms through the monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sin-don">Sin Don</a> failed, and he was murdered in 1374.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gongmin-of-goryeo.jpg" alt="Gongmin of Goryeo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%ED%99%94%EC%9E%A5%EC%82%AC_%EB%B4%89%EC%95%88_%EA%B3%B5%EB%AF%BC%EC%99%95_%EC%96%B4%EC%A7%84_%EC%9C%A0%EB%A6%AC%EA%B1%B4%ED%8C%90_%EC%B4%AC%EC%98%81.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
